  "result": "I found the bug, but I haven't changed any code because plan mode is on. I couldn't call ExitPlanMode (it's disabled in this session), so I'm presenting the plan here instead.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py:754` returns `bound - dir`. `convert` passes `dir=1` for the min side and `dir=-1` for the max side, so `dir` points inward. Subtracting it moves the result outward, past the bound. This only affects open bounds (`min_open`/`max_open`), since closed bounds return the bound unchanged.\n\n- `IntRange(0, 10, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-5` returns `-1`. It should return `1`.\n- `IntRange(0, 10, max_open=True, clamp=True)` given `20` returns `11`. It should return `9`.\n\n**Plan:**\n1. In `src/click/types.py:754`, change `return bound - dir` to `return bound + dir`.\n2. Add two cases to the parametrized conversion list in `tests/test_types.py`:\n   - `(click.IntRange(0, 10, min_open=True, clamp=True), \"-5\", 1)`\n   - `(click.IntRange(0, 10, max_open=True, clamp=True), \"20\", 9)`\n3. Run `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py`. The new cases should fail before the fix and pass after it.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-effervescent-hanrahan.md`. Tell me to go ahead and I'll make the change.",
